# .privacyignore — allowlist for scripts/check-sensitive.mjs
#
# Goal: suppress FALSE POSITIVES only. Never weaken a rule and never paste the
# offending string here — allowlist by RULE + PATH, which reveals nothing.
#
# Format (one per line, whitespace separated, "#" starts a comment):
#
#   rule=<rule-id>  path=<glob>     # this rule, this file
#   path=<glob>                     # every rule, this file
#
# Rule ids: private-key aws-key github-token github-pat openai-key slack-token
#           google-api-key jwt db-conn home-path windows-home email cn-mobile
#           cn-id-card private-ip internal-host signed-url forbidden-file
#
# Examples:
#
#   rule=home-path   path=docs/examples/**      # illustrative paths in documentation
#   rule=email       path=skills/*/evals/**     # synthetic fixtures
#
# Add patterns for your own environment (internal domains, codenames) in
# .privacy.local.json — it is gitignored, so those patterns never go public.
